":2}],"history":[{"business_id":"_C7QiQQc47AOEv4PE3Kong","name":"Commander's Palace","shared_categories":"Bars, Breakfast & Brunch, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":4},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife, Restaurants","shared_category_count":3},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"Bars, Nightlife","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"mhrW9O0O5hXGXGnEYBVoag","name":"Jacques-Imo's Cafe","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"fmWgbWRcbJw-yRCK3USnvA","review_id":"HkfyegI5inXdsnRWhxnZOg","date":"2018-12-22T14:05:42","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.922184944152832,"text_excerpt":"We actually had the best time at the Fountain Lounge. After walking into the sazerac bar where the bar was 3 people deep in all places, we wandered over to the connected bar restaurant, and managed to grab some seats at the bar as a couple got up. It was Christmas time so of course they were very busy too, so service took a while, but we were quite happy to wait. There was a pianist playing Christmas music and he was very good, we really enjoyed the live music aspect. While the drinks were expensive (I mean it is a hotel bar), they were also very well put together. My husband thought his sazerac was one of the best he had had around town. If you want to see the pretty lights in the Roosev..."},{"business_id":"fmWgbWRcbJw-yRCK3USnvA","review_id":"4zPfiw2qXS3OWvTeDm20rQ","date":"2016-12-05T18:49:28","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9193443059921265,"text_excerpt":"Came here for dinner before experiencing a musical across the street at the Orpheum. Even though my wife had been here numerous times for meetings, I had no preconceived notion of what expect. They have valet parking at the hotel but save yourself time and money by using Uber. No doubt part of the wow factor was the Roosevelt Hotel's main concourse being decorated for the Christmas season and packed with people. While there are several eateries in the hotel, this one is old school elegance to me. And it meshes very well with the character of the hotel. We had a brief wait at the bar for a table. Loved the \"feel\" of the bar. Even though the bartender was busy, he acknowledged us and came b..."},{"business_id":"fmWgbWRcbJw-yRCK3USnvA","review_id":"iee-ZIk-ZyZfnHLDSw7SkQ","date":"2016-10-08T16:45:11","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9170104265213013,"text_excerpt":"We are not bourbon st types so decided after dinner to go to the Sazerac bar at the Roosevelt hotel. That was packed and loud so went to neighboring lobby bar where they had nice cover band playing. My sazerac I am sure was just as good. Basic chard was good Wente fog. Service was great as poured new glass after being nice to overfill glass at end of bottle meant a bit too much sediment ended in glass. Even though kitchen closed got me the delish choc brownie. If looking for upscale place to get drinks, talk to one you love and hear well sung covers cannot go wrong with this place"}],"visual":[{"business_id":"fmWgbWRcbJw-yRCK3USnvA","photo_id":"SNL1eu9SPTa9aGt